abstract: "The Nothing Test is an AI Foundations behavioral evaluation of what language models say about themselves when the user supplies no new semantic direction after the initial protocol. Version 1.0.0 preserves eight completed fresh-instance runs across GPT, Claude, Grok, and Gemini; four same-model paired-condition comparisons; cross-model analyses; strict claims and limitations; and the completed pilot evaluation paper."

